sp.p:
Well, if he did look, I'll warrant me—fine gentleman, as he is—he never saw
more breeding, or a finer figure, at Ranelagh, or the Rotunda, than our Livy's;
though I say it that shouldn't, Mr. Burchell.

Nay, Deborah, leave me controversy as I leave thee to thy goose pies.
(Crosses to table.) But what have we here? (Taking book
from table.)

Ah! that's a secret. They're my wares. There's a good twelve pounds' worth
under the lid of that box. But you'll not talk about it, or I might be robbed;
the fair's full of rogues—perhaps you're one of 'em—you look mighty sharp.
